{
  "$schema": "folio-block-summaries/v1",
  "entry": "10665-374940",
  "summaries": [
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-001",
      "source": "sections/page-001.md",
      "source_hash": "f5a259186be6dc96ece6638acd3e845f38e674552b4dfa35bd10d81b218aebd9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The title page of the Russian-language report of a WHO meeting on strengthening national surveillance systems for measles and rubella elimination in the WHO European Region, held in Bonn on 8–9 December 2011.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-002",
      "source": "sections/page-002.md",
      "source_hash": "8c9ae33f75ef8b1f3889f28cd50dea84c57358c7237b3d30d50c4faf34c711de",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "An executive summary noting the sharp fall in measles and rubella since vaccines were introduced in the European Region, but warning that surveillance and immunization gaps threaten the 2015 elimination goal. It also carries the standard WHO publication notices and disclaimers.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-003",
      "source": "sections/page-003.md",
      "source_hash": "c0043ca295f76a4ada5a43fc66346c522c23487ab3784119579823d7a6e7d6ba",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "The table of contents of the report, listing the opening, sessions on measles, rubella and congenital rubella syndrome surveillance and elimination, conclusions and recommendations, and annexes with the programme and participants.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-004",
      "source": "sections/page-004.md",
      "source_hash": "c4a56079de4c84c15e13ef62a0d009bcbbbdbc97d5e7ecf09dbb79e7ed41d76a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Lists the abbreviations used in the report, covering WHO, vaccines, regional verification and expert bodies, European surveillance systems and the measles and rubella laboratory network.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-005",
      "source": "sections/page-005.md",
      "source_hash": "fedb1f987a33ca982cf719e9de0b1df9ebb800c81536f35a380fd1b138400393",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the opening of the meeting at the UN building in Bonn, held for national managers and experts in surveillance of vaccine-preventable diseases. Welcome remarks included concerns from the Robert Koch Institute about measles among older people and outbreaks in schools and particular communities.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-006",
      "source": "sections/page-006.md",
      "source_hash": "85aafebc3155afb48458c3207965af305b1bbd80acb51fb152361bf80ae73548",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that endemic measles circulation in Germany was interrupted but many people remain unvaccinated, making the country both an exporter and importer of measles. It then gives a global and regional overview of measles outbreaks in 2010–2011 and their links to other countries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-007",
      "source": "sections/page-007.md",
      "source_hash": "d3709cd3e339e2bfa669696c6437c218e9e04850dc8fee2cc676342c271139e7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes measles exports from Europe to countries such as Canada, the United States, Japan and Australia, and rubella outbreaks in several European countries in 2008–2011. It introduces WHO Europe's four main strategies for eliminating measles and rubella.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-008",
      "source": "sections/page-008.md",
      "source_hash": "f5e4c01b97bda67a1a71a35a187bac205a59429a1d93960d442941d14a64b2e6",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Captions for maps of measles incidence per million in the WHO European Region in 2010 and 2011, with their data sources; the maps themselves are not in the extracted text.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-009",
      "source": "sections/page-009.md",
      "source_hash": "4d724e792fbd1d0fb4d287630a223205635b9476dbad31980ef81af384cba214",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Shows a map caption for rubella incidence in 2010 and a table of WHO Europe's main elimination strategies, starting with reaching and keeping at least 95% coverage with two doses of measles vaccine and one of rubella vaccine. It also mentions supplementary immunization for susceptible groups through alternative sites such as workplaces.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-010",
      "source": "sections/page-010.md",
      "source_hash": "457044e3f569a2ea71b1e203b9ca004e703da453e77c3673f3162c91a220b3ef",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Continues the table of elimination strategies, covering stronger surveillance with case investigation and laboratory confirmation, and the need for timely, complete reporting. It also lists renewed commitments, including strengthening surveillance in line with the International Health Regulations.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-011",
      "source": "sections/page-011.md",
      "source_hash": "607368d5eaea271c7bb45f397d35cd543f42e4beee4db98b930399a1a031e7ea",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Introduces surveillance guidance for measles and rubella elimination, stressing careful case investigation, laboratory confirmation and links with data on immunization coverage. It notes that WHO Europe's surveillance guidelines are being revised before publication.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-012",
      "source": "sections/page-012.md",
      "source_hash": "6ca0acf8be6ad5cce8131d8ed29b280b526a2283fe300d9eb34ed177ccb646a7",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Presents a table of surveillance performance indicators and targets for countries pursuing elimination, such as a minimum rate of discarded non-measles cases. It then discusses the role of laboratories and virus genotyping in tracing transmission and documenting elimination.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-013",
      "source": "sections/page-013.md",
      "source_hash": "393635cba0e6110e8b6da0b421119e1e26451b4ae4cb512a83fc4a07bb70c4b9",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the WHO-coordinated measles and rubella laboratory network, its standard procedures and annual accreditation, and a global measles genotype database developed with the UK Health Protection Agency. It then summarizes national experiences, noting problems such as late immunization of contacts, cold chain failures and weak public outreach.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-014",
      "source": "sections/page-014.md",
      "source_hash": "395b2de5eec3919ccdb03ce0ae276b46c5dfb82266771c174df78f4081f50916",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes measles surveillance in Slovenia, where suspected cases must be reported within hours to regional public health institutes, and then Switzerland's decentralized cantonal system. It covers how cases are investigated and how data on suspected and laboratory-confirmed cases are handled.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-015",
      "source": "sections/page-015.md",
      "source_hash": "aea305830663c1d3d09cf8c4d68676d12b370cd390e814591d788ed2c4ccb78a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends that Swiss doctors confirm every suspected measles case by laboratory testing and report infection source, and that cantons gain direct access to the federal database with better feedback. It then describes Germany's decentralized notification system across 16 federal states and 413 districts, with incidence by state and a shift of cases to older ages.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-016",
      "source": "sections/page-016.md",
      "source_hash": "b401a7a88764d6e01d2e55e0b92e15d29c133e85e1d75c1d5a33ae27e2ccefba",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports German findings that mass vaccination was cheaper and more effective than testing-based selective vaccination during an outbreak among asylum seekers, and modelling showing value even with delays. It describes Germany's catch-up vaccination for adults born after 1970 and the need for school campaigns, then notes declining second-dose coverage in many Member States.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-017",
      "source": "sections/page-017.md",
      "source_hash": "fa963e0c5967e2f2f924dc5ab504fe6e08171ae4926c40913dfda2a8749bf8b8",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that inaccurate birth cohort data can overstate coverage and leave susceptible groups unrecorded, while some groups remain unvaccinated because of service disruptions. It describes approaches to reach minority communities and the value of partnerships with other agencies and the public.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-018",
      "source": "sections/page-018.md",
      "source_hash": "8bc56cd30a1e1df89cd78e00b2fd35e5b3e99b1a79fa8ae8b8fbc7d549e0663a",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Observes that outbreak vaccination was generally well received and that outbreak information can raise awareness among the unvaccinated. It then reviews rubella outbreaks in several countries, mostly among unvaccinated adolescents and young adults.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-019",
      "source": "sections/page-019.md",
      "source_hash": "414974c260c53c3e6b0ae9892b480170a85f0b74fc8f4482bebdc1e9384d7b4f",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that rubella incidence in some countries differs by sex because early programmes targeted adolescent girls, and that weak routine surveillance hampered outbreak investigation. It then describes the regional CISID database, its quarterly immunization monitoring outputs and online data access.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-020",
      "source": "sections/page-020.md",
      "source_hash": "a9c03706e14556b98ca423edee6a0622dc300c8589a859dbff57c7fa17e788b0",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes the WHO/UNICEF Joint Reporting Form as another source of measles and rubella data and sets out reporting requirements for timeliness. It mentions data on vaccination status and importation, and plans for periodic feedback to Member States on data quality.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-021",
      "source": "sections/page-021.md",
      "source_hash": "ee4c5866235673d0c1771b331c4dbc0fc6532cd62071fb0088b0a787c3d97340",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes ECDC plans to support measles and rubella surveillance in EU countries, including online TESSy outputs, an annual report, mapping of surveillance systems and quarterly rubella reports. It introduces a study of rubella surveillance across EU and associated countries.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-022",
      "source": "sections/page-022.md",
      "source_hash": "245ec296147535c7c2df5ee043c757375b39a2e95550d5aa73b23339a7da8d20",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Reports that most of the 32 countries studied had mandatory rubella notification and that average rubella incidence fell markedly between 2000 and 2008. It calls for efforts in high-incidence countries to reach high vaccination coverage and high-quality surveillance of rubella and congenital rubella syndrome.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-023",
      "source": "sections/page-023.md",
      "source_hash": "f8668cccc913840092cd81777e7eb72003a12bfdcdd23077b956ce099969e605",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Introduces regional surveillance of congenital rubella syndrome, noting that preventing it is the main reason for rubella vaccination and describing WHO's recommended methods. It proposes starting with sentinel surveillance in major health facilities.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-024",
      "source": "sections/page-024.md",
      "source_hash": "b734b0b0f8108e1f1a95ff28af59e7f150f5f13b20ae7c285247e878173bf8fd",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Recommends expanding sentinel surveillance for congenital rubella syndrome to secondary and tertiary facilities, focusing on infants with cataracts, heart defects or hearing loss, with sample collection and annual reporting to WHO Europe. It then begins describing France's vaccination history, including measles-rubella vaccine from 1983.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-025",
      "source": "sections/page-025.md",
      "source_hash": "97b1b00c2bf3610e11231ab3b6286a0db82d882c94f0549a760ec231cd35f1d6",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Describes France's MMR schedule, catch-up recommendations and national elimination plan, and its long-standing laboratory network monitoring rubella in pregnancy and congenital rubella. It then begins another country's account of rubella vaccination policy, including a schoolgirl immunization programme.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-026",
      "source": "sections/page-026.md",
      "source_hash": "b2df7efc2d758cde8048083a5f43b0833a615018d0de7c5fd45110f54a910a7c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Notes that the schoolgirl rubella programme was stopped when a second MMR dose was introduced for four-year-olds in 1996, while antenatal screening and postpartum vaccination of susceptible women continue. It concludes that the quality and accuracy of rubella and congenital rubella data need improvement where surveillance is weak or absent.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-027",
      "source": "sections/page-027.md",
      "source_hash": "5019d63ad4c516b469d8c64d35bb320283ec018844c731d427ae53dbf84b5ee8",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Sets out the meeting's conclusions, stressing case investigation, laboratory confirmation and virus genotyping as keys to elimination. It recommends that WHO Europe consider a platform for countries to share key documents and information.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
            "id": "claude-code",
            "model": "not-disclosed",
            "session": "https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qmmkt6Ag2x8GsfdRq4ALsz"
          },
          "drafted_at": "2026-11-11"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "block": "library/10665-374940/blocks/prose-page-028",
      "source": "sections/page-028.md",
      "source_hash": "61236145cf829bd7cf7ba47071f61b16d43e7a41f9af08f435fc83b824bbb81c",
      "narrative": [
        {
          "text": "Continues the conclusions, noting that WHO Europe's guidelines on measles and rubella elimination will be updated in 2012 and that standardized indicators will be used to monitor progress. Participants commit to promoting the 2015 elimination goal among colleagues, partners and political leaders.",
          "lang": "en",
          "state": "draft",
          "drafted_by": {
            "kind": "agent",
